clearcote: report bgra8unorm from getPreferredCanvasFormat() for a Windows persona.

Every real Windows Chrome returns bgra8unorm (measured: genuine Chrome 151 on real Windows, and our
own Windows build). Linux returns rgba8unorm because the static GetPreferredCanvasFormat() carries a
mesa BGRA-interop workaround behind #if IS_ANDROID || IS_LINUX, so the value sits beside a renderer
string naming Direct3D11 and contradicts it.

ONLY the V8 binding is patched. The static is deliberately left alone: it feeds
swap_texture_descriptor_.format, so changing it would reconfigure the REAL swapchain rather than the
reported string -- a rendering bug rather than a coherence fix.

Currently cosmetic, since requestAdapter() returns null and nothing can consume the format. Included
because it is one line and correct; it is not a justification for returning an adapter, which needs
967 first.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgpu/gpu.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgpu/gpu.cc
@@ -45,6 +45,8 @@
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/instrumentation/use_counter.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/weborigin/kurl.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/wtf/cross_thread_functional.h"
+#include "build/build_config.h"
+#include "components/ungoogled/persona_profile.h"
 
 namespace blink {
 
@@ -423,6 +425,20 @@
 }
 
 V8GPUTextureFormat GPU::getPreferredCanvasFormat() {
+  // clearcote(r16): a Windows persona reports bgra8unorm, which is what every real Windows
+  // Chrome returns (measured: genuine Chrome 151 on real Windows, and our Windows build).
+  // The static GetPreferredCanvasFormat() below answers rgba8unorm on Linux because of a
+  // mesa BGRA interop workaround (#if IS_ANDROID || IS_LINUX), so the value sits beside a
+  // renderer string naming Direct3D11 and contradicts it.
+  //
+  // ONLY the V8 binding is patched. The static is deliberately left alone: it feeds
+  // swap_texture_descriptor_.format, so changing it would reconfigure the real swapchain
+  // rather than the reported string, which is a rendering bug rather than a coherence fix.
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+  if (ungoogled::GetPersonaPlatform() == ungoogled::PersonaPlatform::kWindows) {
+    return FromDawnEnum(wgpu::TextureFormat::BGRA8Unorm);
+  }
+#endif
   return FromDawnEnum(GetPreferredCanvasFormat());
 }
 
